":"vientiane_wv_cope_visitor_centre","areaId":"vientiane","name":"COPE Visitor Centre","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":17.96127,"lng":102.61789},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"vientiane_wv_cope_visitor_centre","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://www.copelaos.org","official":true}],"signals":{"commonsNearby":15,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["copevisitorcentre","vientiane"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"18:00"}]},"summary":"This centre explores the Lao legacy of unexploded ordnance (UXO) and the National Rehabilitation Centre's efforts to expand prosthetic, orthotic, and rehabilitation services across the country. There are exhibits, and visitors can watch short films on the subject. Exhibits are appropriate for all ages. An excellent gift shop offers fun, offbeat souvenirs that support a good cause. Free parking.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Vientiane","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Mapillary_%28369014081194166%2C_oUxcxVpdgFmjteniEzkEjg%29_%28garok%29_2018-02-14_14H48M20S000.jpg/1280px-Mapillary_%28369014081194166%2C_oUxcxVpdgFmjteniEzkEjg%29_%28garok%29_2018-02-14_14H48M20S000.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Mapillary_%28369014081194166%2C_oUxcxVpdgFmjteniEzkEjg%29_%28garok%29_2018-02-14_14H48M20S000.jpg/500px-Mapillary_%28369014081194166%2C_oUxcxVpdgFmjteniEzkEjg%29_%28garok%29_2018-02-14_14H48M20S000.jpg","w":1200,"h":600,"author":"garok","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mapillary_(369014081194166,_oUxcxVpdgFmjteniEzkEjg)_(garok)_2018-02-14_14H48M20S000.jpg"}},{"id":"vientiane_wv_lao_textile_museum","areaId":"vientiane","name":"Lao Textile Museum","category":"museum","tags":["museums"],"location":{"lat":18.00079,"lng":102.61687},"visitMinutes":120,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"vientiane_wv_lao_textile_museum","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":15,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["laotextilemuseum","vientiane"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"09:00","close":"16:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"16:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"16:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"16:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"16:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"16:00"},{"open":"09:00","close":"16:00"}]},"summary":"A beautiful semi-open-air museum of Lao textiles, clothing, weaving, and dyeing. Watch weavers at work, see samples of traditional Lao clothing, view the process of making indigo and samples of dyed thread, and taste color-changing butterfly-pea flower tea and fresh fruit from the courtyard (included in the ticket price). The gift shop has a lovely selection of silk, cotton, and mulberry paper pro","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Vientiane","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Lao_Textile_Museum_2.jpg/1280px-Lao_Textile_Museum_2.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Lao_Textile_Museum_2.jpg/500px-Lao_Textile_Museum_2.jpg","w":1200,"h":1600,"author":"Mx. Granger","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lao_Textile_Museum_2.jpg"}},{"id":"vientiane_lao_national_museum","areaId":"vientiane","name":"Lao National Museum","category":"museum","tags":["museums"],"location":{"lat":18.00747,"lng":102.64536},"visitMinutes":120,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"vientiane_lao_national_museum","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":2,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-21"},"hashtags":["laonationalmuseum","vientiane"],"hours":{"week":[null,{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"10:00","close":"18:00"}],"note":"Closed Mon; Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"Formerly the Lao Revolutionary Museum. There are 5 exhibition rooms. Impressive architecture of the new museum from the outside, along with artifacts of the country’s prehistoric, wartime, political, and ethnic identity.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Vientiane","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/64/LaosNationalMuseum.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/64/LaosNationalMuseum.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"neajjean","license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LaosNationalMuseum.jpg"}},{"id":"vientiane_wv_chokdee_cafe_restaurant_belgian_beer_bar","areaId":"vientiane","name":"Chokdee Café Restaurant & Belgian Beer Bar","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":17.96307,"lng":102.60583},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"vientiane_wv_chokdee_cafe_restaurant_belgian_beer_bar","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"https://www.facebook.com/Chokdee-Café-119290841456796","official":true}],"signals":{},"hashtags":["chokdeecaferestaurantbelgianbeerbar","vientiane"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"10:00","close":"23:30"},{"open":"10:00","close":"23:30"},{"open":"10:00","close":"23:30"},{"open":"10:00","close":"23:30"},{"open":"10:00","close":"23:30"},{"open":"10:00","close":"23:30"},{"open":"10:00","close":"23:30"}]},"summary":"Restaurant & beer bar, owned by a friendly Belgian citizen who speaks a good English and so does the staff. Their signature meal, which is the Belgium national one, is mussels & fries, with different flavors to choose from, starting at 95,000 kip (US$11). Some finger food such as mini cheese burgers (35,000 kip). Famous for its beers too, including trappist ones, with around 100 different crafted ","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Vientiane"},{"id":"vientiane_wv_dai_japanese_restaurant","areaId":"vientiane","name":"Dai Japanese restaurant","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":17.96579,"lng":102.60481},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"vientiane_wv_dai_japanese_restaurant","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://www.facebook.com/japaneseizakayadai","official":true}],"signals":{},"hashtags":["daijapaneserestaurant","vientiane"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"11:00","close":"22:30"},{"open":"11:00","close":"22:30"},{"open":"11:00","close":"22:30"},{"open":"11:00","close":"22:30"},{"open":"11:00","close":"22:30"},{"open":"11:00","close":"22:30"},{"open":"17:00","close":"22:30"}]},"summary":"Japanese restaurant with a Japanese owner and chef, Takashi, who is friendly and speaks an excellent English. Very large selection (sushi, sashimi, miso soup, gyoza, tempura, teriyaki, soba, udon, ramen, curry, taiyaki) and drinks (Asashi beers, sake, potato schochu, rice shochu, shochu sour [which can be confused with fruit juice — watch out if you don't drink alcohol]). Japanese TV on to feel ev","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Vientiane"},{"id":"vientiane_wv_kong_view_bar_and_restaurant","areaId":"vientiane","name":"Kong View Bar and Restaurant","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":17.96769,"lng":102.58048},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"vientiane_wv_kong_view_bar_and_restaurant","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["kongviewbarandrestaurant","vientiane"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"With the ongoing construction of the flood management levee and river park in Vientiane, this restaurant offers the most optimal dining views of the Mekong. Thai-owned, it features an extensive menu of what is best termed Thai-Lao fusion. Not incredibly exciting food, but good, although portions are on the small side. Also, the staff will invariably mess up your order. Keep a close eye on the bill","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Vientiane"},{"id":"vientiane_wv_osaka","areaId":"vientiane","name":"Osaka","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":17.96451,"lng":102.60549},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"vientiane_wv_osaka","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["osakavientiane","vientiane"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"08:00","close":"20:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"20:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"20:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"20:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"20:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"20:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"20:00"}]},"summary":"Japanese restaurant. Well located. Incredibility large offer of Japanese food (sushi, sashimi, miso soup, gyoza, tempura, teriyaki, soba, udon, ramen, oden, curry, takoyaki, okonomiyaki, tempura ice-cream) and drinks (green tea, cream soda, sake, Asashi beers, plum wine, shōchū ...) Every item on the menu comes written in English, along with its picture (& price). Many item pictures can as well be","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Vientiane"},{"id":"vientiane_wv_papillon","areaId":"vientiane","name":"Papillon","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":17.96419,"lng":102.60416},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"vientiane_wv_papillon","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"https://www.facebook.com/Papillon-French-Restaurant-1725094451131288","official":true}],"signals":{},"hashtags":["papillonvientiane","vientiane"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"18:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"18:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"18:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"18:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"18:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"18:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"18:00","close":"22:00"}]},"summary":"French restaurant owned and managed by an experienced French cook, who used to be the Western French cook at Novotel. Speaks English, and so does his staff. Features traditional food and chef specials, such as andouillettes, rognons blancs (mutton testicles) and tripes à la mode de Caen. There's a 3-course \"Menu of the day\" in addition to the main menu, for 45,000-65,000 kip. Drinks include French","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Vientiane"},{"id":"vientiane_wv_samlo_pub","areaId":"vientiane","name":"Samlo Pub","category":"nightlife","tags":["nightlife"],"location":{"lat":17.96596,"lng":102.60447},"visitMinutes":90,"photoSeed":"vientiane_wv_samlo_pub","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["samlopub","vientiane"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"bestLight":"night","summary":"Once this was one of only a few bars in town, and was packed every evening, especially between 23:00-02:00 after other bars around town are closed. Perhaps quieter now that there is more competition. Has a pool table and shows sports, but the background music often drowns the TV commentary. Drinkers from Bor Pen Nyang often come here when it closes, then move on again to the Don Chan Palace nightc","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Vientiane"},{"id":"vientiane_wv_xang_khoo","areaId":"vientiane","name":"Xang Khoo","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":17.96506,"lng":102.60827},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"vientiane_wv_xang_khoo","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["xangkhoo","vientiane"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"08:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"23:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"23:00"}]},"summary":"Crêperie - Lao French Bistrot. Owned by a friendly French citizen who speaks great English. Staff can as well communicate in English. Mix of Western (mainly French) food with Asian (mainly Lao). Galettes (French buckwheat pancakes) are their signature food and are gluten free (starting at 45,000 kip; they also have pizza, salads, soups. Different desserts such as crepes indeed. Drinks: French wine","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Vientiane"},{"id":"vientiane_wv_privet","areaId":"vientiane","name":"Privet","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":17.93275,"lng":102.62453},"visitMinutes":75,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"vientiane_wv_privet","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"https://www.facebook.com/privetrestaurant/menu/","official":true}],"signals":{},"hashtags":["privetvientiane","vientiane"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"11:00","close":"21:00"},{"open":"11:00","close":"21:00"},{"open":"11:00","close":"21:00"},{"open":"11:00","close":"21:00"},{"open":"11:00","close":"21:00"},{"open":"11:00","close":"21:00"},{"open":"11:00","close":"21:00"}]},"summary":"Classical range of Russian/ex-Soviet dishes, staples and specialties alike, served amid amusingly mixed ambience with various Soviet paraphernalia lining the walls. A rare chance to taste authentic Russian soft drinks like kvass, kefir and mors, or Russian alcohol. Run and staffed by Russian expats.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Vientiane"},{"id":"vientiane_wv_khop_chai_deu","areaId":"vientiane","name":"Khop Chai Deu","category":"nightlife","tags":["nightlife"],"location":{"lat":17.96451,"lng":102.6075},"visitMinutes":90,"photoSeed":"vientiane_wv_khop_chai_deu","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://www.khopchaideu.com","official":true}],"signals":{},"hashtags":["khopchaideu","vientiane"],"hours":{"week":[{"open"